        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "6"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count by parity",
        "body": "A sum of two integers is odd exactly when one is odd and the other even. If $k$ of the four numbers are odd, the number of odd sums is $k(4-k)$ (an odd number paired with an even one).\n\n$k=0,1,2,3,4$ give $0,3,4,3,0$. The maximum is $4$.\n\nIt is reached, for example, by $X=1,Y=3,Z=2,W=4$: the sums are $4,3,5,5,7,6$, and four of them are odd.\n\n**Answer: (C) 4**"
      }
    ],
