    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Carl wrote a list of 10 distinct positive integers on a board. Each integer in the list, apart from the first, is a multiple of the previous integer. The last of the 10 integers is between 600 and 1000. What is this last integer?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "640"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "729"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "768"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "840"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "990"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count prime factors",
        "body": "Each number after the first is a multiple of the previous one and is different from it, so it is at least $2$ times as big. Going from the first to the tenth number we multiply by nine whole numbers, each at least 2. So the last integer is a multiple of a product of nine integers that are each at least 2, and therefore has at least $9$ prime factors (counted with multiplicity).\n\n- $640=2^7\\cdot5$: 8 prime factors.\n- $729=3^6$: 6.\n- $768=2^8\\cdot3$: 9.\n- $840=2^3\\cdot3\\cdot5\\cdot7$: 6.\n- $990=2\\cdot3^2\\cdot5\\cdot11$: 5.\n\nOnly $768$ has at least 9. It is possible: $1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,768$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 768**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
